## Why This Is Asked

Webhook delivery from external providers is inherently unreliable: duplicates, retries, and reordering are common. This question probes practical test strategies that ensure data integrity and idempotency across asynchronous paths.

## Key Concepts

- Idempotency keys and deduping
- Signature verification (HMAC)
- Retry/backoff handling with 429/503
- Out-of-order event handling
- End-to-end ledger consistency and downstream effects

## Code Example

```javascript
// Signature verification (example)
const crypto = require('crypto');
function verifySignature(payload, signature, secret) {
  const hmac = crypto.createHmac('sha256', secret);
  hmac.update(payload, 'utf8');
  return hmac.digest('hex') === signature;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you simulate out-of-order delivery and duplicates in an automated test suite?
- What changes would you make to migrate from at-least-once to exactly-once processing in this webhook path?

## Why This Is Asked

